# Every file here is LF, on every platform that checks it out.
#
# The tests read this repository's own sources and match patterns anchored to
# "\n" -- the usage block in main.go, the job list in ci.yml, the release
# blocks in .goreleaser.yaml -- so git's autocrlf default on Windows would
# have them measuring the checkout rather than the file. The configs bothy
# generates are LF for the same reason: the tools reading them are the same
# tools on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named rather than left to git's content sniffing: a screenshot rewritten as
# text is a screenshot nobody can open.
*.png binary
